ഒന്നാം ഘട്ടത്തിലെ പരിശോധന.

Hamlet, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Juliet, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Romeo, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Othello, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Macbeth, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Lady Macbeth, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ophelia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Cordelia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Desdemona, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Portia, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Viola, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Prospero, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Miranda, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.
Ariel, കണക്കിന്റെ അവസ്ഥ സൂക്ഷിക്കുന്ന കഥാപാത്രം.

Act I: കണക്കിന്റെ പ്രധാന ഘട്ടം.

Scene I: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Ariel and Hamlet]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Ariel and Juliet]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Ariel and Romeo]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Ariel and Othello]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Ariel and Macbeth]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Ariel and Lady Macbeth]
Ariel:
 Listen to your heart.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Miranda]

Miranda:
 You are a hero.

Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between a big big big big big big big hero and a hero.

Scene III: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

Prospero:
 Are you better than nothing?

Miranda:
 If not, let us proceed to scene IV.
 You are as good as the product of yourself and a big hero.

Prospero:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 Let us return to scene III.

Scene IV: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

Miranda:
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.

[Exeunt]

Scene V: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Ophelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the sum of the product of Juliet and Juliet and the product of the sum of a big hero and a hero and Romeo and Hamlet.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene VI: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Cordelia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the sum of the product of Romeo and Romeo and the product of the sum of a big big hero and a hero and Othello and Juliet.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene VII: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Desdemona]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the sum of the product of Othello and Othello and the product of the sum of the sum of a big big hero and a big hero and a hero and Macbeth and Romeo.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene VIII: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Portia]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the sum of the product of Macbeth and Macbeth and the product of the sum of a big big big hero and the sum of a big hero and a hero and Lady Macbeth and Othello.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene IX: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Prospero and Viola]
Prospero:
 You are as good as the sum of the sum of the product of Lady Macbeth and Lady Macbeth and the product of the sum of the sum of a big big big hero and a big big hero and a hero and Juliet and Macbeth.
 You are as good as the difference between yourself and a hero.
 You are as good as the remainder of the quotient between yourself and Prospero.
 You are as good as the sum of yourself and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene X: കണക്കിന്റെ ഉപഘട്ടം.

[Enter Hamlet and Ophelia]
Hamlet:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Hamlet and Cordelia]
Hamlet:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Hamlet and Desdemona]
Hamlet:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Hamlet and Portia]
Hamlet:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]

[Enter Hamlet and Viola]
Hamlet:
 Open your heart.
[Exeunt]
